    <!--
      #0E6B4F is LightPrimary from ui/theme/Color.kt, not a colour picked for the icon.
      It used to be #14624B, which was the primary before the light palette was revised for
      contrast; the icon was simply never moved across, so the launcher and the store art
      were a revision behind the app they belong to. Color.kt records the same drift on
      DarkInversePrimary. If primary changes again, change this with it.

      The sand foreground stays #F0D69A: against #0E6B4F it is 4.57:1, which still clears
      WCAG AA for text. The design's own sand (#E4D2B4, the hero gradient's last stop) is
      only 4.38:1 on this green — fine for a graphic, but this mark is read as a glyph and
      there was no reason to spend the margin.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#0E6B4F"
        android:pathData="M0,0h108v108h-108z" />
</vector>
